// dos_progs.logic — the programs on the virtual drive
//
// These are real 8086 machine code, assembled from source and stored here as
// bytes. The emulator loads them like any other .COM: they set video modes
// through INT 10h, write to VGA and text memory through segment registers,
// talk to the DAC through OUT, read the keyboard through INT 16h and exit
// through INT 20h/21h. Nothing about them is simulated at a higher level.
//
//   HELLO.COM   prints through INT 21h AH=09h
//   PLASMA.COM  mode 13h field, animated by cycling the DAC palette
//   MANDEL.COM  Mandelbrot in 16-bit fixed point (IMUL/SHRD), drawn in place
//   BOXES.COM   CP437 line drawing straight into B800:0000

